# Custom form fields (golden rule)

When adding **new entry** flows (create/edit modals) in any module or feature, the platform must support **tenant-defined custom fields** configurable by **store admin**, **superadmin**, and **owner** roles.

## Who can configure

- `store_admin`, `superadmin`, `owner` (tenant-scoped; respect RLS and module permissions)

## Supported field types (minimum set)

| Type | Control |
|------|---------|
| Short text | textbox |
| Long text | textarea |
| Single choice | radio, dropdown |
| Multi choice | checkbox group |
| Number | number input |
| Number range | min/max pair |
| Date | date picker |
| Date range | start/end date pickers |

## Implementation expectations

1. **Schema** — per-entity custom field definitions (label, type, options, required, sort order) stored per tenant.
2. **API** — CRUD for field definitions (admin+ only); read definitions on list/get; validate and persist values on create/update.
3. **UI — Settings page** — admins manage custom fields on the feature **Settings** page (`EntityFormSettingsPage`), not inside create/edit modals. See `.cursor/rules/form-field-settings.mdc`.
4. **UI — modals** — use `CustomFieldsSection` from `web/src/shared/CustomFieldsSection.tsx` inside every create/edit `EntityModal` (render values only). Admins configure fields via the **cog icon** beside **+ New row** on each grid (not in the header nav).
4. **Grids** — optional: show high-value custom columns when configured; keep sort/filter rules explicit per field type.

New features must not hard-code a closed field set only — plan for the custom-field extension point from the start.
